  "readme": "# Mimi105 complete visible-process comparison\n\nThe same retained V5 lossless MKV now has one complete471-frame RGB decode, with50duplicate adjacent packet PTS, actual EOF/exit0 and all pre-encoder/raw/decoded-showinfo Adler and PTS checks. The V3 metadata parser preserves interleaved original stderr fragments by original byte spans;46rawmuxer warnings remain. This validates extraction, not restoration fidelity.\n\nTwo independent reviewers covered all471actual frames/40contact sheets and all126source frames/5sheets, with full-size native witnesses. Both reject full-process acceptance: the actual first visible pose is already raised and lacks the earlier visible lower-to-higher hand phase; actual376→377 disappearance differs from the source fade. No body/face fields are installed.\n\nMouth correction: original61 has no final note/diamond and is closed;62 has both and is still closed;63–64 open, and no later closed mouth was observed through106. Earlier wording implying repeated completed-hold mouth cycling is explicitly withdrawn in the addenda. Actual186completes/open and later holds open. Japanese/Chinese text lengths and distinct clocks must be separated; no lip-engine cause is inferred.\n\nAfter complete review, all41native witness PNGs used by either reviewer (plus boundary endpoints), all40contact sheets, the original MKV and full hash/PTS logs remain.430other generated PNGs were retired, freeing229871616bytes, with exact compact retirement manifest; no replacement media backup. Historical full-index image paths may now be retired.\n\nThe original captured program and movie are already bound by the B8 audit at4de5d91d; they are not duplicated here. Native data, resources and canonical front end remain unchanged by this audit-only publication.\n"
